course: dictionary
lesson: 3797
title: Forbidden: not allowed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Forbidden means not allowed, usually by a rule or a law. You will see it on signs and in school rules. «Strictly forbidden» means there is no choice at all: you must not do it.
explain: Forbidden can also describe something you are told not to have or go near, and that can make it seem tempting. In old stories, the «forbidden fruit» is the thing you are told to leave alone, so everyone wants it. Notice the feeling: a forbidden thing often hints at danger or trouble.
explain: Check the context. «The Forbidden City in Beijing was the palace of Chinese emperors from 1420 until 1912, and it is now a museum.» The name tells you that ordinary people were not allowed inside. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Ordinary people were not allowed in the palace» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Forbidden means not allowed, especially by a rule or law.
fact: «Forbid» means to say no to something, and «forbidden» is its past participle, as in «It is forbidden to feed the animals.»
fact: «Strictly forbidden» means there is no exception at all.
fact: In fairy tales, a «forbidden door» or «forbidden forest» often leads to trouble.
fact: «Défense de marcher sur la pelouse» means «Keep off the grass», where «défense de» means «it is forbidden to».
exercise: «Défense de marcher sur la pelouse» means «Keep off the grass». What does défense de mean? | Please come in | The grass is wet | *It is forbidden to | The lawn is big
exercise: A school sign says «Building site: strictly forbidden». What does strictly forbidden mean? | *Not allowed, with no exceptions | Free to visit if you ask nicely | Only for teachers | Allowed on a sunny day
exercise: «Visitors are forbidden to feed the animals.» What does forbidden mean here? | Free | Invited | *Not allowed | Hungry
exercise: «The Ming dynasty, from 1368 to 1644, moved the capital to Beijing and built the Forbidden City.» Which dynasty built the Forbidden City? | A French gardener | *The Ming dynasty | The Forbidden Forest | The Roman army
exercise: A fairy tale says «Do not open the forbidden door.» Why might the door seem tempting? | Because it is painted gold | Because nobody has ever seen a door | Because it is very small | *Because it is forbidden, so people want to know what is behind it
test: The legend says the Forbidden City has 9,999 rooms, but surveys count about 8,700. What is the legend's idea behind the number 9,999? | It is a very small number | It is the number of children in Beijing | *Only Heaven can have 10,000 rooms | It is the year the palace was built
test: Which word in «It is forbidden to walk on the grass» could be swapped for «not allowed» without changing the meaning? | *forbidden | walk | the | grass
exam: Which word means the opposite of forbidden? | Tempting | *Allowed | Hidden | Ancient
